<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec tin imports up 7.7 pct year/year--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec tin imports up 7.7 pct year/year--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 2,050 tonnes of refined tin in December, up 7.7 percent from 1,903 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>			Dec 96	   Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		2,050	    1,935	    1,903</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	  1,048	    1,019		639</p>
<p> Malaysia	     497		459		570</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in 1996 were 25,272 tonnes, off 9.8 percent from 28,019 tonnes the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 6179</p>
</text>
